? How do visitors reach this site
  > Through a Cloudflare Tunnel (no public ports; DNS on Cloudflare)
    Directly, on ports 80 and 443 (Caddy gets the certificate)
  Create a tunnel in the Cloudflare dashboard and copy its token, the long
  string in the install command it shows. It is saved to
  /etc/vps-ready/cloudflared-token, readable only by root, for the connector to
  read at each start.
? Tunnel token (hidden; Enter to add it later): [hidden]
  That is not a tunnel token: copy it from the install command in the Cloudflare
  dashboard.
? Tunnel token (hidden; Enter to add it later): [hidden]
  No port is opened: cloudflared connects out to Cloudflare, and Caddy listens
  on loopback only.

After you apply, you have 5 minutes to log in from a new terminal and confirm.
If you don't, every change is undone.

